# escape_gate_tethra -- the gate to Tethra's court under the wave (east): steps going down into the swell to a drowned
# gate. What it shows, and why there is no way through.

@file underworld/escape
@encounter 7

= the gate
@continue
Sea-worn stone, crusted with shells and the white of old salt.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
Seal-folk are carved either side, their faces turned toward the water.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
The steps go down to a gate half under the tide, rusted and barnacled:
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
the heave and the fall, the heave and the fall, the water running back between the stones.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]

= where it goes
This way runs down to Tethra, king under the wave.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
No one that has gone down those steps has come back up from them.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
That much is known. That much, and no more.
% [Gaeilge le teacht]
